1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,840
- Woo!

2
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:05,760
Ready?

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
- Well, good morning, guys.

4
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:00,840
Welcome, church.

5
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:01,660
I turned it on.

6
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:02,960
Danny always asks me if I remember what to do

7
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:04,900
and I always tell him no, so.

8
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:06,060
Good morning, Canvas community.

9
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:07,620
For those of you that might not know me,

10
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:10,700
my name is Corey Smith and I have the privilege

11
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:14,180
of being on the teaching team here at church.

12
00:01:14,180 --> 00:01:17,000
This morning, I have the huge honor and privilege

13
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,680
of preaching through Revelation four and five.

14
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:23,480
And if you couldn't tell, I'm pretty pumped about it.

15
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:27,340
But first, I wanna extend my thanks to Taylor

16
00:01:27,340 --> 00:01:32,100
for her excellent reading, for Ryan and Donovan.

17
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:34,420
If anybody sees Donovan, give him a pat on the back

18
00:01:34,420 --> 00:01:37,480
'cause I think I stressed him out this morning.

19
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:42,960
For them giving into my thoughts around this passage

20
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:46,680
because honestly, this vision has shaped so deeply

21
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:48,800
my love for Christ and his church.

22
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:51,540
And I wanna invite us into that vision

23
00:01:51,540 --> 00:01:53,820
as we wrestle with John's vision

24
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:56,460
and the implications it might have for us.

25
00:01:56,460 --> 00:02:00,560
Church, I want us this morning to stand in solidarity,

26
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:02,360
not physically stand, you don't have to stand again,

27
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:06,360
but with John and the seven churches and see.

28
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:10,420
Not to decode, not to speculate,

29
00:02:10,420 --> 00:02:13,820
not to escape the world, but to see.

30
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:17,920
Because that is what Revelation is doing.

31
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:20,100
Like we've talked about, Apocalypse is kind of this idea

32
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:21,540
of a peek behind the curtain.

33
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:23,880
And for many of us, Revelation was handed to us

34
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:25,800
as a strange book about future events

35
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:28,440
and a mixed book of timelines, charts, codes,

36
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:32,020
beasts, marks, and predictions.

37
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:35,080
And because of that, many Christians either become obsessed

38
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:36,680
with Revelation or avoid it altogether.

39
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:38,640
And I want us to find that space

40
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:41,440
because I think some approach it with fear,

41
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:43,580
some with curiosity, some approach it

42
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:45,240
as if it were a puzzle to be solved.

43
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:47,160
But I want to echo Dr. De Silva here,

44
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:48,820
if you were with us during his lecture,

45
00:02:48,820 --> 00:02:50,720
we want to approach Revelation

46
00:02:50,720 --> 00:02:53,040
in the best way we can

47
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:55,080
alongside the original audience.

48
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:59,140
Before John sees what is coming against the church,

49
00:02:59,140 --> 00:03:02,800
John is shown who reigns over the church.

50
00:03:03,540 --> 00:03:05,640
And I think the order of that matters.

51
00:03:05,640 --> 00:03:08,860
Revelation 4 and 5, I think, often gets the cue of like,

52
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:10,440
this is the pause before the action.

53
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:13,360
But I would argue that this is the engine

54
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:15,400
by which the whole book runs.

55
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:18,080
It is the interpretive center.

56
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:20,500
If we miss Revelation 4 and 5,

57
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:22,320
we will misread everything else.

58
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:24,560
Because the crisis in Revelation

59
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:27,200
is not that Jesus might lose the throne.

60
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:29,300
The crisis in Revelation is the church

61
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:30,540
might forget who sits on it.

62
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:33,540
So John is writing to real churches

63
00:03:33,540 --> 00:03:35,960
in real places under real pressure.

64
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:38,520
These churches living in the shadow

65
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:39,640
of the Roman Empire.

66
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:43,640
Because Rome, if you're a student of history like I am,

67
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:44,720
has its own gospel.

68
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:45,880
It has its own good news.

69
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:47,420
It has its own lords.

70
00:03:47,420 --> 00:03:49,680
It has its own peace, right?

71
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:50,620
Pax Romana.

72
00:03:50,620 --> 00:03:53,260
It has its own liturgy, symbols, ceremonies,

73
00:03:53,260 --> 00:03:56,300
claims about what is true and what is reality.

74
00:03:56,300 --> 00:04:01,180
Rome says, Caesar is Lord.

75
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:04,980
Rome says, peace comes through power.

76
00:04:04,980 --> 00:04:09,560
Rome says, security comes through violence.

77
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:12,320
Rome says, if you want to survive,

78
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:14,220
you will learn how to accommodate.

79
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:17,100
I'll let you draw your own parallels there.

80
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:20,600
But into that world, John is given a vision.

81
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:22,780
Not a vision of a someday throne,

82
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:24,260
not a vision of a future victory

83
00:04:24,260 --> 00:04:25,640
that may or may not happen.

84
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:27,120
No, John is given the unveiling

85
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:28,840
of what is already true.

86
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:30,880
Revelation 4, 1 says,

87
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:31,960
after this and I looked

88
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:33,680
and there in heaven was an open door.

89
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:35,900
The first voice that I heard

90
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:37,540
speaking to me like a trumpet said,

91
00:04:37,540 --> 00:04:40,420
come up here and I will show you

92
00:04:40,420 --> 00:04:42,060
what must take place after this.

93
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:45,640
So I want us to kind of take our time

94
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:46,660
as we go through here.

95
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:48,400
John sees an open door.

96
00:04:50,080 --> 00:04:52,500
Now you've heard me harp on this imagery before.

97
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:53,680
And when we hear heaven,

98
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:55,720
I think many of us instinctively,

99
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:59,040
even subconsciously imagine a far off place

100
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:00,120
somewhere above the clouds,

101
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:01,580
somewhere distant,

102
00:05:01,580 --> 00:05:03,600
somewhere detached from earth,

103
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:05,100
somewhere we go after we die.

104
00:05:05,100 --> 00:05:07,540
And that's not really the picture

105
00:05:07,540 --> 00:05:08,680
Revelation has given us.

106
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:12,320
John is not being invited to escape reality.

107
00:05:12,320 --> 00:05:14,000
No, I would argue John is being invited

108
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,140
to see reality at its deepest,

109
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:17,520
most true level.

110
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:19,940
Heaven is not far off

111
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:21,620
in a place in sense of distance.

112
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:25,200
Heaven is something beyond this.

113
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:27,720
Heaven is the unveiled dimension

114
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:29,880
of reality where God's reign

115
00:05:29,880 --> 00:05:30,840
is fully seen,

116
00:05:30,840 --> 00:05:31,960
fully confessed,

117
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:33,180
and fully worshiped.

118
00:05:33,180 --> 00:05:35,960
It's a place beyond Rome's propaganda.

119
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:37,960
It's beyond the church's fear.

120
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:39,380
It's beyond the suffering

121
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:40,560
that seems final.

122
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:43,440
It's beyond the powers

123
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:44,140
that appear

124
00:05:44,140 --> 00:05:45,980
to rule this world.

125
00:05:45,980 --> 00:05:49,060
It's beyond everything

126
00:05:49,060 --> 00:05:50,540
that looks so permanent,

127
00:05:50,540 --> 00:05:51,660
so threatening,

128
00:05:51,660 --> 00:05:53,260
and so immovable.

129
00:05:53,260 --> 00:05:55,340
And what does John see?

130
00:05:55,340 --> 00:05:57,380
Revelation 4, 2,

131
00:05:57,380 --> 00:05:58,800
immediately I was in the spirit

132
00:05:58,800 --> 00:05:59,860
and there was a throne

133
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:00,840
in heaven

134
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:01,860
and someone

135
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:03,160
was seated on it.

136
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:04,600
There

137
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:06,100
was a throne.

138
00:06:06,100 --> 00:06:07,800
Now there will be a throne,

139
00:06:07,940 --> 00:06:08,700
not someday God

140
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:09,460
will take the throne,

141
00:06:09,460 --> 00:06:10,440
not someday after everything

142
00:06:10,440 --> 00:06:11,120
gets bad enough

143
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,820
Jesus will finally become Lord.

144
00:06:12,820 --> 00:06:13,460
No,

145
00:06:13,460 --> 00:06:15,000
there was a throne

146
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:15,680
and someone

147
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:17,280
was already seated on it.

148
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:18,540
Church,

149
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:20,000
that one sentence

150
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,280
may be the heart of Revelation.

151
00:06:21,280 --> 00:06:22,480
If you are a note taker,

152
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:23,260
write this down.

153
00:06:23,260 --> 00:06:24,360
There is a throne,

154
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:26,040
the throne is occupied,

155
00:06:26,040 --> 00:06:28,120
and God alone reigns supreme.

156
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:31,060
Heaven is not panicking.

157
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:33,100
The elders surrounding the throne

158
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:34,400
are not wringing their hands.

159
00:06:34,400 --> 00:06:36,800
The throne is not fragile.

160
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:39,120
The throne is occupied,

161
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:40,120
and the throne

162
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:41,180
and around the throne

163
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:41,780
is worship.

164
00:06:41,780 --> 00:06:44,540
John sees the living creatures

165
00:06:44,540 --> 00:06:45,540
and day and night

166
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:46,780
they never stop saying,

167
00:06:46,780 --> 00:06:47,380
Holy,

168
00:06:47,380 --> 00:06:47,900
Holy,

169
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:48,460
Holy,

170
00:06:48,460 --> 00:06:49,860
Lord God Almighty

171
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:50,620
who was,

172
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:51,360
who is,

173
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:52,420
and who is to come.

174
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:54,820
And the elders fall

175
00:06:54,820 --> 00:06:55,600
before the ones

176
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:56,540
seated on the throne,

177
00:06:56,540 --> 00:06:58,340
cast their crowns

178
00:06:58,340 --> 00:06:58,940
before him

179
00:06:58,940 --> 00:06:59,540
and say,

180
00:06:59,540 --> 00:07:01,220
Our Lord and God,

181
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:02,200
you are worthy

182
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:04,080
to receive glory

183
00:07:04,080 --> 00:07:05,180
and honor and power

184
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:06,300
because you created

185
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:06,880
all things

186
00:07:06,880 --> 00:07:07,900
and by your will

187
00:07:07,900 --> 00:07:08,960
they exist

188
00:07:08,960 --> 00:07:10,140
and were created.

189
00:07:10,140 --> 00:07:12,620
This is not just

190
00:07:12,620 --> 00:07:13,660
beautiful imagery.

191
00:07:13,660 --> 00:07:15,460
This is a confrontation

192
00:07:15,460 --> 00:07:16,680
of what the empire

193
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:17,260
is saying.

194
00:07:17,260 --> 00:07:19,400
Because Rome said

195
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:20,620
Caesar was worthy.

196
00:07:20,620 --> 00:07:22,060
Because Rome said

197
00:07:22,060 --> 00:07:23,340
empire is glorious.

198
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:24,880
Because Rome says

199
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:26,640
the powers of this world

200
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:27,960
demand your allegiance

201
00:07:27,960 --> 00:07:28,860
but heaven says

202
00:07:28,860 --> 00:07:29,160
no,

203
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:31,420
the Lord God Almighty

204
00:07:31,420 --> 00:07:32,240
is worthy.

205
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:33,920
Worship,

206
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:34,820
if you don't know,

207
00:07:34,820 --> 00:07:36,400
is the act

208
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:37,520
of ascribing worth

209
00:07:37,520 --> 00:07:40,220
to the one

210
00:07:40,220 --> 00:07:41,720
who is actually worthy.

211
00:07:41,720 --> 00:07:44,060
Worth-ship

212
00:07:44,060 --> 00:07:44,800
or worship

213
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:46,220
is the response

214
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:46,920
of creatures

215
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:47,700
like you and I

216
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:48,860
who have recognized

217
00:07:48,860 --> 00:07:49,940
the worthiness

218
00:07:49,940 --> 00:07:51,400
of their creator.

219
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:53,260
Christian worship

220
00:07:53,260 --> 00:07:54,660
in all of its forms

221
00:07:54,660 --> 00:07:55,680
should tell the truth

222
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:56,700
to the world around us.

223
00:07:56,700 --> 00:07:58,340
This is why

224
00:07:58,340 --> 00:07:59,580
worship of creator God

225
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:00,680
is not an escape

226
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:01,400
from reality.

227
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:02,320
Worship is not,

228
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:03,980
worship is participating

229
00:08:03,980 --> 00:08:05,660
in the deepest reality.

230
00:08:05,660 --> 00:08:06,820
It is not closing

231
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:08,160
our eyes to suffering

232
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:09,480
but instead opening

233
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:10,800
our eyes to the throne.

234
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:13,460
It is not taking a break

235
00:08:13,460 --> 00:08:14,360
from the real world

236
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:14,920
on Sundays.

237
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:15,700
I'm gonna take a break

238
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:16,060
for an hour.

239
00:08:16,060 --> 00:08:16,860
I'm gonna go to church.

240
00:08:16,860 --> 00:08:18,560
That's where everything's good.

241
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:18,960
No,

242
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:20,600
it is learning

243
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:21,640
or maybe better said

244
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:22,360
reorienting

245
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:23,460
or unveiling

246
00:08:23,460 --> 00:08:24,640
the world

247
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:25,740
to see the world

248
00:08:25,740 --> 00:08:26,900
the place

249
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:27,960
where God's reign

250
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:29,100
is already recognized

251
00:08:29,100 --> 00:08:29,780
and the lamb

252
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:31,000
is already worshipped.

253
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,560
This is where

254
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:33,300
we need to recover

255
00:08:33,300 --> 00:08:34,720
something the ancient church

256
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:35,460
often understood

257
00:08:35,460 --> 00:08:36,280
better than we do.

258
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:38,180
In many historic

259
00:08:38,180 --> 00:08:39,000
Christian traditions

260
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:39,800
corporate worship

261
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:40,580
is not treated

262
00:08:40,580 --> 00:08:41,740
like in a religious event

263
00:08:41,740 --> 00:08:42,680
we do on Sunday mornings.

264
00:08:44,680 --> 00:08:46,360
Worship is treated

265
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:47,880
as participation

266
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:49,900
the co-mingling

267
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:51,040
of heaven

268
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:52,000
and earth

269
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,560
in one grand

270
00:08:53,560 --> 00:08:54,720
cosmic event.

271
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:56,200
An invitation

272
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:56,860
to participate

273
00:08:56,860 --> 00:08:58,080
in what is already

274
00:08:58,080 --> 00:08:59,200
happening around the throne.

275
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:00,320
The church

276
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:01,300
does not create

277
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:01,980
the reality

278
00:09:01,980 --> 00:09:02,760
of God's kingdom.

279
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:03,980
No.

280
00:09:03,980 --> 00:09:05,620
We don't even have

281
00:09:05,620 --> 00:09:06,900
to imagine the reality

282
00:09:06,900 --> 00:09:08,440
but we're invited

283
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:09,900
into this reality

284
00:09:09,900 --> 00:09:11,140
that we cannot see.

285
00:09:11,140 --> 00:09:12,560
In faith

286
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:13,200
in allegiance

287
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:13,900
to the lamb

288
00:09:13,900 --> 00:09:14,820
the church

289
00:09:14,820 --> 00:09:15,980
steps into that faith

290
00:09:15,980 --> 00:09:16,720
bears witness

291
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:17,180
to it

292
00:09:17,180 --> 00:09:19,620
and bears witness

293
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:20,540
to the supremacy

294
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:21,180
of the lamb

295
00:09:21,180 --> 00:09:22,260
and is forged

296
00:09:22,260 --> 00:09:23,580
by its allegiance

